--- 5b. USER FLOW NETWORK (Edmonds-Karp) -----------------------
  Flow network : 8 nodes, 10 edges
  Source       : Source
  Sink         : Sink

  Edge capacities:
      Source       -> V1            16.00 t/day
      Source       -> V2            13.00 t/day
      V1           -> V2            10.00 t/day
      V2           -> V1             4.00 t/day
      V1           -> V3            12.00 t/day
      V2           -> V4            14.00 t/day
      V3           -> V2             9.00 t/day
      V4           -> V3             7.00 t/day
      V3           -> Sink          20.00 t/day
      V4           -> Sink           4.00 t/day

  Maximum feasible throughput : 23.00 t/day

  Minimum cut (bottleneck edges):
      V1           -> V3            12.00 t/day   <-- SATURATED
      V4           -> V3             7.00 t/day   <-- SATURATED
      V4           -> Sink           4.00 t/day   <-- SATURATED

  Maximum flow : 23.00 t/day
  Minimum cut  : 23.00 t/day
  Verified: max-flow = min-cut (max-flow/min-cut theorem holds).

================================================================
  Dijkstra chooses efficient paths.  Greedy prioritises urgent
  bins.  Dynamic programming respects truck capacity.  Max-flow
  exposes infrastructure bottlenecks.  One coordinated framework.
